00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:17.770
- I'm from Spain.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:18.685
- You're from Spain?

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:19.518
- Yeah.

00:00:19.518 --> 00:00:20.530
- You came to, the United
States at what age?

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:24.210
- About six months maybe less.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.260
- Just when you were very young--

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.380
- Yeah, I was raised in Los Angeles.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.457
- In Los Angeles, okay.

00:00:30.457 --> 00:00:32.550
And you had both your parents?

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:33.930
- Well, they're deceased now.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.090
- Yeah, but growing up
you had both your, uh?

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.180
- Yeah, we started out as a family

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.550
you know, but, things happened.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:42.530
- Yes.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:44.820
Did your parents separate at some point?

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:47.710
- Well, my father died when I was two.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:48.780
- Oh my God!

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:49.613
- Pneumonia.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.223
He had a one lung left.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:56.203
- Oh my God!

00:00:56.203 --> 00:00:59.000
So, did your mom remarry or?

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.578
- She remarried.

00:01:00.578 --> 00:01:01.550
(motorcycle engine roaring)

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:05.655
Unfortunately, the wrong persons for her,

00:01:05.655 --> 00:01:09.143
but, she has about two
or three more husbands.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:13.220
- And so, how was you childhood?

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.280
- It was very religious.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.331
I went to a Catholic
school for eight years.

00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:22.208
- Oh, really!

00:01:22.208 --> 00:01:23.337
- It's not there now,

00:01:23.337 --> 00:01:27.793
but, it was for the first to eighth grade.

00:01:30.535 --> 00:01:31.750
- And your childhood was good,

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.550
no abuse, anything like that?

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:36.000
- Well, there was some abuse over there.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.880
They were run mostly by nuns

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:44.380
and one nun in the fifth
grade, she was the worst.

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:48.353
It was a physical abuse actually.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:54.480
Yeah, she would slap the pupils

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.429
that didn't learn fast enough

00:01:56.429 --> 00:02:00.530
(mumbles) or make him sit
at the edge of a desk.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:01.960
You know, punishment like that.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:02.793
- Right.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:07.270
- I didn't like it.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:11.143
That was the only thing I
didn't like about the school.

00:02:11.143 --> 00:02:13.623
Was the strict nuns.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:18.243
- So later on, did you go to college?

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.760
- I went to Santa Monica City College.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.650
- Okay, and where'd you go--

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:25.483
- Didn't graduate though.

00:02:25.483 --> 00:02:27.610
Just had a couple of semesters.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:30.420
- And how was your work, career,

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.198
Are you still working?

00:02:32.198 --> 00:02:34.490
- Yes, as a matter of fact, I am.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:36.260
Just temporarily.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:37.093
- Okay.

00:02:37.093 --> 00:02:40.100
What did you do throughout
your career for jobs?

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:43.470
- Well, I went to the ranches

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.593
to learn how to ride a horse, yeah.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:51.280
And, from there I went to a ranch

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.123
owned by somebody from Arizona, a cowboy.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:58.920
He raised horses there
then he trained them

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.092
and got them ready to go to the racetrack.

00:03:01.092 --> 00:03:06.092
So, I got paid 25 a month
and room on board though

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.233
and there was 15 of us.

00:03:12.233 --> 00:03:14.180
- Oh!
- Everybody had their own room

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:19.473
and, they worked throughout
the ranch, training the horses.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.360
And when they got ready,

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:26.083
the trainer at the ranch would
send them to his racetrack.

00:03:29.444 --> 00:03:32.250
- What other jobs did you have later on?

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.003
- I drove a bus for the RTD,

00:03:35.598 --> 00:03:37.410
at the time it was called RTD

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:43.223
and I was there about
three years, you know.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:47.880
After that I went to Texas for a year,

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:51.670
and worked, in the...

00:03:52.746 --> 00:03:54.573
I was the second cook.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:56.910
In other words, I did all the baking.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:59.130
- Okay.
- You know,

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:02.893
and they were grooming
me to be a first cook.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:08.803
And I was looking forward
to that 'cause I like food.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:14.470
But, it didn't work out cause
I had to come back here.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:16.331
My girlfriend was..

00:04:16.331 --> 00:04:18.483
Had trouble with her baby,

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:21.810
